*.md
# ...except this one. `Dockerfile` copies it because `pyproject.toml` declares
# `readme = "README.md"`, and pip refuses to build package metadata without the
# file the metadata points at.
#
# Found by running the build for the first time: `*.md` excluded it, the COPY at
# Dockerfile:21 could not find it, and the production image failed to build. The
# Dockerfile was consistent with the repository and inconsistent with what the
# build context actually contained — which is a thing no amount of reading
# either file would reveal.
!README.md
__pycache__
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
*.mp4
node_modules
dist
dist-test
